.Dd October 24, 2026
.Dt AUGITE-REPO 1
.Os Augite DEVEL
.
.Sh NAME
.Nm augite-repo
.Nd generate a static site for a Git repository
.
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm "augite repo"
.Oo
.Fl o
.Ar dir No \&|
.Fl "-output"
.Ar dir
.Oc
.Oo
.Fl g
.Ar dir No \&|
.Fl "-grammars"
.Ar dir
.Oc
.Oo
.Fl c
.Ar dir No \&|
.Fl "-cache"
.Ar dir
.Oc
.Oo
.Fl p
.Ar number No \&|
.Fl "-per-page"
.Ar number
.Oc
.Oo
.Fl u
.Ar url No \&|
.Fl "-base-url"
.Ar url
.Oc
.Oo
.Fl "-parent"
.Ar path
.Oc
.Ar repo-dir
.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm "augite repo"
generates a site for the Git repository at
.Ar repo-dir .
The site includes a paginated commit log,
commit diffs,
the files at HEAD,
branches,
tags and Atom feeds.
Repository metadata can be set with
.Xr augite-setup 1 .
.Pp
The output directory is created if necessary and defaults to
the current directory.
Log pages,
file pages,
references,
feeds,
the stylesheet and JavaScript are updated on each run.
Pages for files no longer in the tree and log pages beyond the
last page are removed.
.Pp
Commit pages are written only when they do not already exist.
To regenerate all commit pages after an upgrade,
remove the output directory’s
.Eo
.Pa commit/
.Ec
subdirectory and run the command again.
.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Fl o ,
.Fl "-output"
.Ar dir
.Xc
Writes the site to
.Ar dir
instead of the current directory.
.It Xo
.Fl g ,
.Fl "-grammars"
.Ar dir
.Xc
Uses TextMate grammars in
.Ar dir
to highlight file pages.
Without this option,
file pages are plain text.
To add a language,
copy its
.Ql "\&.tmLanguage\&.json"
file into the directory.
.It Xo
.Fl c ,
.Fl "-cache"
.Ar dir
.Xc
Keeps highlighted files in
.Ar dir
between runs to avoid highlighting them again.
The directory is created if necessary.
Changes to the grammars invalidate cached highlighting.
Unused cache files are removed after a run.
.It Xo
.Fl p ,
.Fl "-per-page"
.Ar number
.Xc
Sets the number of commits per log page.
The default is 50.
The number must be a positive integer.
.It Xo
.Fl u ,
.Fl "-base-url"
.Ar url
.Xc
Sets the site’s base URL,
used to make links in the Atom feeds absolute.
For example,
.Ql "https://code\&.example\&.org/engine/" .
Without this option,
feed links are relative.
This is separate from the clone URL set by
.Xr augite-setup 1 .
.It Xo
.Fl "-parent"
.Ar path
.Xc
Links each page to the list of repositories at
.Ar path ,
such as one written by
.Xr augite-index 1 .
A relative
.Ar path
is relative to the site’s root,
so
.Ql "\&.\&."
is the directory above it.
An absolute path or a URL is used as is.
The link appears above the header and on the logo.
Without this option,
pages do not link outside the site.
.It Xo
.Fl h ,
.Fl "-help"
.Xc
Prints a usage summary and exits.
.El
.
.Sh FILES
Paths below are relative to the output directory.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Eo
.Pa ./index.html
.Ec ,
.Eo
.Pa ./log.html
.Ec ,
.Eo
.Pa ./log/<number>.html
.Ec
.Xc
The commit log.
The first page is written to both
.Ql "index\&.html"
and
.Ql "log\&.html" ;
subsequent pages are written under
.Eo
.Pa log/
.Ec .
.It Xo
.Eo
.Pa ./commit/<hash>.html
.Ec
.Xc
Individual commit pages.
.It Xo
.Eo
.Pa ./files.html
.Ec ,
.Eo
.Pa ./file/
.Ec
.Xc
The file listing and individual file pages.
.It Xo
.Eo
.Pa ./refs.html
.Ec
.Xc
Branches and tags.
.It Xo
.Eo
.Pa ./atom.xml
.Ec ,
.Eo
.Pa ./tags.xml
.Ec
.Xc
Atom feeds for the latest 100 commits and for tags.
.It Xo
.Eo
.Pa ./style.css
.Ec ,
.Eo
.Pa ./augite.js
.Ec
.Xc
The stylesheet and JavaScript used by the site.
.It Xo
.Eo
.Pa ./logo.png
.Ec ,
.Eo
.Pa ./favicon.png
.Ec
.Xc
Images linked by the pages.
Augite does not create these files;
supply them separately.
.El
.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Generate a site with syntax highlighting and a persistent highlighting
cache:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ augite repo -o public/engine -g grammars -c cache/engine \e
    -u https://code\&.example\&.org/engine/ --parent \&.\&. \e
    /var/git/engine\&.git
.Ed
.Pp
To rebuild after pushes,
run the command from the repository’s
.Eo
.Pa hooks/post-receive
.Ec
hook.
The project includes an example in
.Eo
.Pa res/hooks/post-receive
.Ec
that also rebuilds the repository index.
.
